+
+#### Human-attended issuance broker
+
+`issue-live-host-challenge.py --matrix-cell CELL --issuer-key-id KEY_ID
+--nonce-ledger PATH --trusted-signers PATH` accepts only the five existing
+cells and existing regular repository files. It offers no override for nonce,
+time, issuer, schema, executable, signer, or key material. It invokes canonical
+A1 with fixed argv, derives UTC `issued_at`, preserves the existing issuer
+literal as generator identity, presents the existing unsigned five-field entry
+and raw digest, and reads one canonical-base64 Ed25519 signature line. It never
+reads or invokes a private key.
+
+Before append it re-reads and validates registry and ledger, rejects duplicates
+or registry drift, enforces wall-clock and monotonic deadlines, and verifies the
+registered issuer-role signature. Issuance and consumption share `PATH +
+".lock"`; the broker appends under that lock with the existing temp, fsync, and
+atomic-replace discipline and never removes another process's lock. stdout stays
+empty until durable append, then carries only unchanged A1 challenge JSON.
+Pre-append failure leaves the ledger unchanged; post-append delivery failure
+keeps the entry and requires fresh issuance. Exit categories are 0 durable
+issuance, 2 input/schema, 3 trust/signature, 4 lock/storage, 5 A1 generation,
+and 6 expiry/interruption. No outcome is a native verdict, approval, signature,
+two-party record, or AC-028 discharge.
+
+This section supersedes only the stale issuer/write descriptions at
+investigation.md:46, tasks.md:838, and any task text that describes A1 as the
+ledger writer. Those frozen artifacts remain byte-unchanged in this candidate;
+their task-stage wording must be reconciled only after the amended design gate.
